
❯ Explain in one sentence why terminal width matters for multiline composer detection. Next
  I will ask you to outline a detailed regression test plan for wrapped suggestions and
  multiline drafts.

● Terminal width determines where the terminal soft-wraps long lines, so a single logical
  line (a wrapped suggestion or draft) can appear as several visual rows, and detection that
  reads the screen row by row can mistake those wrapped continuation rows for a multiline
  draft (or a real multiline draft for a wrapped suggestion) unless it accounts for the
  current width.
 
  Ready for the regression test plan whenever you are.

